From 16d61dcd203d0190290d34359c824c684539013f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 10:39:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] MIG-1 follow-up: MIG-24 T1 (Primitives) and T3, seal
 repairs

T1, Primitives part: the private catalogRewind was statement-identical to
the public Turing.FinTM.timed_rewind; it is retired and its four call
sites use timed_rewind. T3: the twelve frame-exactness side proofs of
emCall_bank_initial / emCall_bank_final now cite two private lemmas,
emCall_pair_not_mem and emCall_triple_not_mem. CertShell and
CodeSimulator read the canonical seam's state through Cfg.ofWords_state
instead of rfl. Primitives: several moved forwarding-map and poly-space
steps read runFrom 0 / runFrom 2, initCfg and Action.apply through the
published equations.
---
